# ============================================================================
# SORREL JUNCTION  (rail-hub city, 28x23 blocks, buffer 986/1300) johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: the crossroads of Johto's railways. The Magnet Train main line
#   runs straight through town on a fenced double track, a freight siding
#   peels off east into the Goods Yard, and the whole city lives by the
#   timetable: porters, switchmen, freight clerks and the commuters who
#   ride to Goldenrod and Marigold every morning. Sorrel Central is the
#   grandest station in Johto. During the Eclipse the Signal Tower goes
#   dark, the points jam and every train in Johto stops at Sorrel.
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door steps in obj warp lines)
#   Freight Row (north of the tracks, rows 1-3)
#     Warehouses 1 and 2 (3x2 brown roofs, 08 7b 09 / 1c 16 1e)  2 is the
#                                   locked one with the stolen cargo
#     Coal shed (2x2 brown, blind 7c 7d wall, no door)
#     Freight Office (3x2)          foreman; delivery side-quests
#     Signal Tower (2x3 grey tower) the plot building: switch puzzle inside
#     Switchman's house, Porter's house, kiosk (67)
#   The Main Line (rows 4-7): 49 fence / two 7e tracks / 41 fence, crossed
#     only at the brick Northgate crossing (cols 5-6) and the Yard crossing
#     (cols 22-23); 7f is the level-crossing block, as in Goldenrod
#   Sorrel Central Station (8x4, cols 10-17): roof abuts the track like
#     Goldenrod's station; two doors - Ticket Hall (W) and Arrivals (E);
#     interior leads up onto the platforms (Magnet Train + local lines)
#   Goods Yard (east, rows 8-13): siding (rows 9-10) running off the E edge
#     into the goods shed (blind brown 2x2), its own yard crossing, Freight
#     Depot (3x2 brown) and Rail Workers' cottage
#   Station Square (brick, rows 11-13): street trees, two signs (station /
#     timetable board), taxi and newspaper NPCs
#   Northgate Road (brick, cols 5-6): N exit -> crossing -> Platform Street;
#     Bike & Scooter shop (3x2), commuter homes
#   Platform Street (row 14): brick W-E high street, W and E exits
#   Sorrel Market (brick, cols 11-16, rows 15-21): three rows of stalls
#     (67 kiosks, 12 in all) - berries, apricorns, rail-souvenirs, a fish
#     cart, a rotating "freight surplus" stall that sells odd items
#   Commuter Row (SW): terraces (14 13 + 67) and three 2x2 homes
#   Market Side (SE)
#     Sleeper Car Inn (4x2)         PC in the lobby + paid rest; replaces a
#                                   Pokemon Center
#     Market Hall (3x2 brown)       covered market / auction of lost cargo
#     Florist, tailor and homes; small grove (SE corner)
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive on Platform Street; the Inn is next to the market.
#   2. Every train is held: the Signal Tower lost power and the points are
#      jammed. The Signalman's door is locked; the key is with the
#      Freight foreman, who wants the stolen cargo found first.
#   3. Market gossip -> Warehouse 2 -> thieves (cult grunts) -> cargo + key.
#   4. Signal Tower interior: lever/points puzzle, boss on the top floor.
#   5. Trains run: Sorrel Central sells the Rail Pass (fast travel between
#      Goldenrod, Marigold and the other line); freight surplus stall and
#      market auction unlock.
#
# EXITS / CONNECTIONS
#   N  Northgate Road (cols 5-6)      to a northern route
#   S  Market Street (cols 13-14)     to a southern route
#   W  Platform Street (row 14)       toward Marigold City
#   E  Platform Street (row 14)       toward the eastern route
#   Rails leave the map at rows 5-6 (W and E) and rows 9-10 (E siding): the
#   neighbour maps must continue the 7e track (or end it in a tunnel/fence).
#   30 building doors, all listed below and reachable on foot.
#
# TILE GAPS / UNCERTAIN BLOCKS
#   - Track is E-W only (7e/7f): no N-S track, curve, points/switch,
#     buffer stop or platform-edge block, so the siding just runs into the
#     goods shed and the platforms live inside the station.
#   - 7f crossing shows light ground, not brick, even on Northgate Road
#     (Goldenrod has the same look).
#   - No crate/container, water tower, lamp post or clock block; the
#     signal box uses the grey radio-tower art.
#   - Wide brown roofs use 7b as the middle roof piece; 1c 16 1e under it
#     shows a faint line left of the door (16's left edge). 7c/7d (blind
#     orange walls) are only used as end pieces.
#   - 2c is the plain yellow wall used between the station's doors.
#   - Market stalls are 67 (one-block houses), as in silkwater.
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 p=2f
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a F=0f O=16 W=1e C=1c K=33
key 1=14 2=13 g=27 m=23 G=28 c=2c
key j=25 J=26 y=29 Y=2a d=2d k=2e
key 9=08 0=09 B=7b [=7c ]=7d
key ==7e #=7f f=41 e=49 s=45 S=77 w=66
grid:
TTTTT::TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT
TRN.h::.9B0.9B0.90.RMN.jJRNT
TOW.h::.COW.COW.[].EFZ.yYOWT
T....::........p.......dk..T
Teeee::eeeeeeeeeeeeeee..eeeT
=====##===============##====
=====##===============##====
Tffff::fffRMMMMMMNffff..fffT
T....::...gmmmmmmG..ee..eeeT
TRN.h::RN.gmmmmmmG90==##====
TOW.h::OW.AcDccDcZ[]==##====
T....::.::::::::::::ff..fffT
TRMN.::.:w::::::::w:RN.9B0.T
TADZ.::.:S::::::::S:OW.COW.T
::::::::::::::::::::::::::::
T.12h12h12.h:hh:h.RMMN.RN..T
T..p..p..p.::::::.EFFZ.OW..T
TRN.RN.RN..h:hh:h..........T
TOW.OW.OW..::::::.9B0.RN.ppT
T..........h:hh:h.COW.OW.,,T
T.12h12h12.::::::.h.12.h12.T
T..........::::::..........T
TTTTTTTTTTTTT::TTTTTTTTTTTTT
end
